cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Joeyyy: a brain-locked, fail-closed governance system for multi-agent runtimes"
message: "If you use or build on these governance patterns, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Elder
    given-names: Joe
    alias: JoeElder21
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoeElder21/Joeyyy"
license: Apache-2.0
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  An agent governance system implementing cross-brain separation with a single
  authorized cross-brain governor. Two mirrored specialist units (APEX for
  professional context, JEOS for personal context) share a functional class
  taxonomy but are isolated in prompts, evidence, memory namespaces, write
  targets, and roundtables, and may not communicate directly.

  The reusable contribution is the enforcement layer rather than the roster:
  typed delegation, handoff, memory, and writer-lease packet contracts validated
  as JSON Schema; fail-closed packet admission that rejects malformed or
  out-of-mode requests; one designated writer per canonical brain/target/resource
  with lease-serialized mutation, schema-valid readback, and recorded rollback;
  staged shadow-to-active acceptance gating with a hard human checkpoint before
  activation; user-signed one-time launch grants for write-capable mounts; and a
  provenance-verified capability absorption protocol hardened against
  repository-impersonation supply-chain attacks.

  Governance rules are executable rather than advisory: the documentation,
  templates, registry, and schemas are asserted to agree by the test suite, and a
  privacy guard enforces the public-repository data boundary on every commit.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent governance
  - ai safety
  - least privilege
  - policy enforcement
  - model context protocol
  - supply chain security
  - land development engineering
